(pass) seal/open round-trips text and 4 KB of bytes, and each seal is different [22.30ms]
(pass) a sealed message that was altered, cut, or sealed to another key is refused, never garbage [21.47ms]
(pass) bundle round-trips at the default cost, and unlock finishes in under 6 s [10401.09ms]
(pass) the header carries m, t, p and a fresh salt, readable without the passphrase [1661.81ms]
(pass) a wrong passphrase fails cleanly [147.33ms]
(pass) a tampered bundle is refused: damaged in copying, altered on purpose, or asking for too much work [224.28ms]
(pass) a bundle of an unknown version, or not a bundle at all, says so [28.24ms]
(pass) a bundle pasted with line breaks and spaces unlocks, and the passphrase is Unicode-normalised [49.02ms]
(pass) the async pair round-trips, and gives byte-identical bundles to the sync pair for the same salt [4695.43ms]
(pass) without setTimeout the async pair falls back to the sync path, with the same output [129.78ms]
(pass) the async pair fails with the same faults as the sync pair [370.89ms]
(pass) passphrase strength scores and explains, and only warns [2.44ms]

